%description:
Tests that the ACK of a time-wait socket carries no AccECN option either, as
the ACK of Linux tcp_v4_send_ack(), which writes only the timestamp option.
The scenario is that of tcp_accecn_10 with the AccECN option of Linux: the other
segments carry the option, and the ACK in TIME_WAIT carries none.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 1000"
*.*_tcp.accEcnOptionEnabled = true
*.*_tcp.accEcnOptionPolicy = "linux"
*.*_tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn"
*.cli_app.tClose=2s
*.srv_app.tClose=3s
*.*_tcp.accEcnBareTimeWaitAck = true

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[3.001 B004] A.1000 < B.2000: A F E N ack 1002 win 16384   Option(s): NOP AccECN1(e1b=1,ceb=0,e0b=1001)
cli_tcp: FIN_WAIT_2 --> TIME_WAIT  (on RCV_FIN)
[3.003 A005] A.1000 > B.2000: A ack 502 win 16384 
srv_tcp: LAST_ACK --> CLOSED  (on RCV_ACK)
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
